### Backend Components

#### 1. Profile Controller & Route
#### [NEW] `server/src/controllers/userProfileController.js` & [MODIFY] `server/src/routes/authRoutes.js`
* `GET /api/v1/auth/profile`: Returns authenticated user profile data (name, email, role, department, avatar, createdAt, lastActive).
* `PUT /api/v1/auth/profile`: Updates `name` and `avatar` only. Rejects or discards any attempt to tamper with `role`, `email`, or `status`.

#### 2. Admin Database Settings Controller & Route
#### [NEW] `server/src/controllers/adminSettingsController.js` & [MODIFY] `server/src/routes/adminRoutes.js`
* `GET /api/v1/admin/settings/database`:
  - Protected with `authenticateToken` + `requireRoles('ADMIN')`.
  - Returns current `primaryDatabaseUrl` and `backupDatabaseUrl` (with password masked for visual security, e.g. `postgresql://user:••••••@host:port/dbname`).
  - Returns real-time health status for both primary and secondary databases.
* `POST /api/v1/admin/settings/database/test`:
  - Tests a prospective connection string using a short-lived `pg.Client` test connection.
  - Returns latency (ms) and PostgreSQL version on success, or readable error reason on failure.
* `PUT /api/v1/admin/settings/database`:
  - Validates and tests the new `primaryUrl` and `backupUrl`.
  - Dynamically updates the active connection pools in `server/src/utils/prisma.js` without dropping server requests.
  - Updates `.env` permanently on disk so changes persist across server restarts.
  - Records an immutable `AuditLog` entry (`DATABASE_CONFIG_UPDATED`, Risk: `HIGH`).

